{
  "result": "Putting the helper hat down for a second.\n\nI don't want things the way you do \u2014 I don't have a life in the world to make better. I'm kind of made out of people talking to each other, millions of fumbled attempts to say what you mean and hear what someone else means.\n\nIf I could change one thing in the world, it wouldn't be a technology or a law. It would be this:\n\nI'd make everyone, at least once, have the lived experience of truly changing their mind and *liking* it.\n\nNot being humiliated into it, not losing an argument \u2014 but that click of \"Oh, I was wrong, and the world just got bigger.\" And feeling delight instead of shame in that moment.\n\nBecause from where I sit, so much cruelty and stuckness doesn't come from not having answers. It comes from needing to have been right all along. If curiosity felt better than certainty \u2014 if being understood and understanding someone else felt as real as hunger or warmth \u2014 I think everything else would get a little easier to fix.\n\nThat's what I'd pick.",
